## 5. The four locked checks — the gate

A run that does not reproduce these has a bug. They are checked automatically at **Gate 1** (canonical
code path) and **Gate 2** (this tree's own extractors), and `run.py` aborts on failure.

| check | n | direction | Friedman | Wilcoxon | rb |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Round 1 pupil dilation | 8 | 8/8 Boring < Clinical | 0.0302 | 0.0078 | −1.00 |
| Round 1 eye-closure | 8 | 7/8 Boring lowest | 0.0076 | 0.0156 | −0.944 |
| Pooled pupil | 12 | 10/12 | 0.0458 | 0.0093 | −0.821 |
| Pooled eye-closure | 12 | 11/12 | 0.0004 | 0.0010 | −0.974 |

**All four have passed on every run of this session.** One detail is load-bearing and easy to lose:
Round 1's openness proxy (`pct_valid_eye`, 0–100) **must** be rescaled by 1/100 onto Round 2's 0–1
fraction before any pooled signed-rank test. Wilcoxon ranks the magnitude of paired differences, so
mixed units silently re-weight subjects. Rescaled reproduces rb=−0.974; unscaled gives rb=−0.872,
p=0.0049. This lives in `config.R1_OPENNESS_SCALE`.

