## 7. Findings so far

**Confirmed and stable**

- **Pupil and eye openness are the two surfaces that carry the result.** 9 pairwise contrasts survive
  Holm across the entire analysis, and every one of them is pupil or openness.
- **Openness is the strongest effect in the dataset.** Pooled N=12: Boring below Interesting in **12/12**
  subjects (rb=−1.00, Holm p=0.0015) and below Clinical in 11/12 (rb=−0.974, Holm p=0.0020).
- **EEG is not significant anywhere.** 0 of 5 surfaces reach Friedman p<0.05; 0 of 15 pairwise contrasts
  survive Holm; keystone concordance is 4/8, exactly chance. Retention averages 62.3% (range
  36.3–74.4%, 3 of 24 cells below 50%). This is the evidence for the "dropped because too noisy"
  ruling, and it is reported rather than asserted.
- **S05's sleep event is directly visible** as a single continuous **449-second** eye closure beginning
  245 s into the Boring episode.
- **Prior exposure resolves 4/12** (S02, S03, S08 by `(Med)` marker; R2-01 by explicit statement) and
  the strata remain near-indistinguishable on clinical — boredom 6.00 vs 5.13, engaged composite 0.286
  vs 0.277. The exposure objection is still answered at N=12.

**Discovered this session, and each one changes something**

- **Round 2 openness is BINARY**, not continuous. Across 12 cells and 3,416,362 per-eye samples the only
  values present are {0, 1}. The specification describes it as continuous; it is not. Consequence: the
  threshold is irrelevant and the blink/extended-closure split rests **entirely** on the VanderWerf
  duration ceiling.
- **A headset on/off artefact in Round 2.** Nine of twelve cells put their longest closure in the final
  3% of the recording; all twelve are 27–36 s. Round 2 has no crop export, so its full recordings
  include non-wear time that Round 1's crop windows exclude. Worth 2.4–3.0 percentage points of "eye
  closed" per cell. Trimmed columns added; **conclusions identical either way**.
- **S06's harmonisation flips its direction on gaze variance.** Round 1 gaze variance moves from
  Friedman p=0.6065 (4/8) to p=0.3247 (5/8) — still not significant, but the artefact is gone. The
  within-Round-1 decimation factors (0.72×, 0.76×) land inside the 0.65–0.84 band measured across
  rounds, independently confirming the no-pooling rule.
- **The zero-reverse asymmetry does NOT hold at N=12.** See §8 — this is the most consequential finding
  and it weakens a claim the specification expected to strengthen.
- **A new divergence case in Round 2**: R2-02's Interesting episode carries the S07 signature (boredom 7
  *and* engagement 6). Full divergent set at N=12: S02, S04, S07, S08, R2-02.
- **Round 2 does have HRV**, contrary to the recon note — 11 files, 10 of 12 cells usable. Excluded
  anyway by author ruling, but the record needed correcting.
- **Blink rate is not recoverable in Round 1.** Its median sampling interval is ~334 ms, which is the
  mean spontaneous blink duration. A blink occupies 0–1 samples. Blink rate is a Round 2 measure only.

---

## 8. The reverse case — read this before writing anything

The specification asks whether the zero-reverse asymmetry holds at N=12. **It does not.** The clinical
decomposition is:

| category | n | subjects |
|---|---|---|
| divergent (physiology engaged, self-report bored) | 5/12 | S02, S04, S07, S08, R2-02 |
| concordant-engaged | 3/12 | S01, S03, R2-04 |
| concordant-bored | 3/12 | S05, S06, R2-01 |
| **reverse** | **1/12** | **R2-03** |

Three things must travel with that number:

1. **It is sensitive to how the engaged composite is built.** Reverse cases number 0 under openness
   alone, 1 under the baseline (pupil + cognitive load + openness), 2 under pupil + cognitive load, and
   3 under pupil alone. R2-03 is reverse under 6 of 7 definitions.
2. **It survives the non-wear trim** (composite −0.510 untrimmed, −0.451 trimmed).
3. **"Reverse" is a within-subject relative statement, not an absolute one.** R2-03 reported boredom
   3/1/2 across the three videos — they never reported being bored by anything, and never became bored
   on any stimulus. Their clinical episode is simply their own relative physiological minimum. That is
   materially different from "physiologically bored while reporting engagement", and the honest form of
   the finding says so without making the case disappear.

