## 9. What remains

### Phase 6 — figure suite (`analysis/figures.py`)

Required set is written out in that file's docstring. In summary: **12 per-subject sets** (summary card,
per-stimulus time series with closures shaded, self-report vs physiology, felt vs actual duration),
**3 combined sets** one per stimulus (distribution with every subject plotted, paired-difference slope
plot, cohort time-series envelope), and **8 cross-cutting figures** (effect-size forest, keystone
scatter, keystone decomposition strip, eye-closure heatmap, R1-vs-R2 replication, felt-duration
dilation, channel correlation matrix, EEG justification).

Every figure: colour-blind-safe fixed stimulus colours from `config.STIM_COLOR`, PDF **and** PNG, a
sibling `.csv` with the same stem carrying its source data, and a caption stub naming n, test,
statistic and effect size. All source data is already computed and available in the `ctx` dict returned
by `run.main()`.

Note: **matplotlib exists only in `.venv`**, not in the pyenv interpreter. This is why D7 exists.

### Phase 7 — reproducibility artefacts (`analysis/report.py`)

`RUN-MANIFEST.json`, `METHODS.md`, `EXCLUSIONS.log`, `QC-REPORT.md`, `FINDINGS.md`, `SOURCES.md`,
`RECONCILIATION.md`. Required content is written out in that file's docstring. Two things are easy to
miss: METHODS.md **must print `adapters.WRAPPERS` verbatim** (8 entries, each with its reason), and
every file must be written through `journal.write_text()` so the PII guard runs on the way out.

### Then

Re-run twice and confirm byte-identical CSVs, and confirm `git status --porcelain scripts/boredom-o9/`
is still empty.

---

## 10. Standing constraints — non-negotiable

- **PII.** `S01`–`S08` / `R2-01`–`R2-04` only. No participant name in any output, log, figure, caption
  or filename. The crosswalk is never persisted; it is derived at runtime from sorted folder order via
  `common.subject_map()`. `journal.emit_guard()` is a **backstop, not the mechanism** — redact by
  construction. It fired twice this session: once on a genuine leak (fixed), once on a false positive
  (`bored`, harvested from a video clip filename, exempted explicitly).
- **Never edit `scripts/boredom-o9/`.** Wrap, don't edit; record every wrapper. Currently clean.
- **Never pool a rate-dependent feature across rounds.** Every pooled statistic carries a `poolable`
  flag and a one-line reason.
- **Crop windows only** for Round 1. If a crop is ever missing, fail loudly — never substitute the full
  recording. Enforced before the run in `adapters.run_ch_hmd()`.
- **Nothing is omitted for being non-significant.**
- **No chapter prose. No commits. No video processing.** Back up before touching any existing file, and
  say so first.
- Label every n<6 result **descriptive**; at n=4 the Wilcoxon floor is p=0.125, so perfect separation is
  the strongest obtainable result and must be stated as such.

